      },
      "body": "You could also mention that for 2-of-3 P2SH inputs, having at least one high-r signature increases the input by an additional 2 bytes because the input script’s length indicator then requires three bytes. For 2-of-3 P2SH inputs, roughly 25% of inputs have two low-r signatures and take 293 bytes, about 50% have one high-r signature and take 296 bytes, and 25% of inputs have two high-r signatures that take 297 bytes. So for 2-of-3 P2SH inputs, the expected savings of low-r grinding is 2.5 vB.",
